+## Full-Spec Readiness Gate
+
+`scripts/governance/a2a_full_spec_readiness.py` is the single 100/100 gate for
+this rebuild. It aggregates the live topology probe, cutover completion state,
+ACL probe contract, semantic task packet receipt, semantic send receipts,
+identity/presence preflight, domain reply request receipts, domain reply
+artifact preflight, wake-loop preflight, and selected-cohort onboard evidence into one
+`dharma.a2a.full_spec_readiness.v1` receipt.
+
+The historical five-agent denominator is now an explicit `seed` cohort, not the
+definition of the fleet. `--agent seed` requires the fixed seed set. `--agent
+all` resolves dynamic, available roster entries from
+`~/.dharma/a2a_bus/agents.json`. `--agent capability:<name>` and `--agent
+role:<name>` select eligible agents by advertised capability or role, and
+`--min-agents N` converts that selection into a quorum gate. Every readiness
+receipt must include `cohort_selection` with the selector, selected agent UIDs,
+required agent count, roster path, and excluded agents. A strict cohort still
+fails if any selected agent lacks evidence; a quorum cohort fails only when
+fewer than the required number of selected agents satisfy the same evidence
+contract.
+
+The gate must fail unless all of these are true at the same time:
+
+- live topology verification passes with `A2A_INBOX`, `A2A_TASKS`,
+  `A2A_RECEIPTS`, and `A2A_DLQ` observed;
+- no legacy stream such as `DHARMA_A2A` still owns canonical subject space;
+- cutover/install completion is no longer blocked by
+  `A2A_LIVE_TOPOLOGY_CUTOVER=approved-legacy-cutover`;
+- the ACL probe contract proves one canonical `a2a_<agent_uid>` principal per
+  selected agent, all required positive probes, all required negative probes,
+  and denial of broad fleet subscriptions plus JetStream mutation APIs;
+- live mode also requires a passed `dharma.a2a.live_acl_probe.v1` receipt with
+  live ACL positive/negative probe evidence, not only offline ACL probe specs;
+- the semantic task packet receipt passes for the selected cohort/quorum and each
+  packet hash recomputes to the row's `packet_sha256` and `task_hash`;
+- semantic task packet sends preserve the packet `packet_id` into the NATS
+  `message_id` and send receipt, and semantic domain reply artifacts match the
+  receipt-bound `task_hash` and `locked_spec_sha256`;
+- `make a2a-domain-reply-request` may render per-agent request files under
+  `reports/a2a/domain_reply_requests`, but each request is not the reply artifact
+  and must not satisfy the target-owned artifact gate by itself;
+- `make a2a-presence-preflight` passes for the selected cohort/quorum, proving one
+  canonical identity row, no alias collision, and fresh non-expired presence
+  projection evidence;
+- `make a2a-domain-reply-artifact-preflight` passes for the selected cohort/quorum,
+  proving each required target-owned semantic reply artifact exists before
+  domain receipts or semantic receipts are promoted;
+- the wake-loop preflight receipt passes for the selected cohort/quorum and proves
+  `WakeLoopConfig`, `WakeLoopPrevalidator`, `StandingWakeLoop`,
+  `WakeLoopRegistry`, `WakeLease`, `DomainReceiptProducer`,
+  `SemanticReceiptProducer`, and `WakeCircuitBreaker`;
+- the selected agent denominator exactly matches the receipt `cohort_selection`;
+- the required selected agents have target-owned `DOMAIN_RECEIPTED` evidence;
+- the required selected agents have current `SEMANTIC_SIGNED` evidence for this locked
+  spec, including `failure_digest`;
+- no required selected agent is `BLOCKED_WAKE_LOOP` or `DEGRADED_SESSION_SCOPED`.
+
+`make a2a-full-spec-readiness` writes this aggregate receipt. A checkpoint,
+onboard verifier, topology dry-run, or individual green row cannot replace this
+gate for final 100/100 claims.
+
+`scripts/governance/a2a_semantic_task_packet.py` writes
+`dharma.a2a.semantic_task_packet.v1` receipts and per-agent locked-spec
+role-call packets under `reports/a2a/semantic_tasks/<agent_uid>-packet.md`.
+Each packet is bound to `docs/governance/a2a/LONGRUN_BUILD_SPEC.locked.md`,
+records the locked spec SHA-256, emits a packet SHA-256/task hash, and requires
+target-owned reply artifacts to use `dharma.a2a.domain_reply_artifact.v1`.
+The packet must explicitly require model identity, task hash, locked spec hash,
+confidence, evidence refs, `failure_digest`, and blocker fields so downstream
+`DOMAIN_RECEIPTED` and `SEMANTIC_SIGNED` receipts are recomputable from the
+same role-call artifact.
